RECORDED AS BRAINSTORMING, NOT AS A PROPOSAL. Kept as an idea by @ajs, 2026-10-22: "record A-E as ideas. I think they are things we can use to continue to refine reflow2."

FROM: Terence Tao, "AI views" (teorth.github.io/tao-web/ai-views.html, updated 2026-10-20), read through a summarizing fetch, so quotes may be close rather than exact.
- He decomposes problem-solving into generation → verification → exposition → publication → canonicalization. AI accelerates the first two, so EXPOSITION and digestion are now the scarce steps.
- His red-team test: "if you would be unable to coherently present the output … in a class presentation and … answer questions about it without further AI assistance, it should not be part of your workflow."

WHAT TODAY'S TRIALS SHOWED (heat rung and Lucas–Penrose, 2026-10-22):
- reasoning_report reads BREADTH-FIRST FROM THE THEOREM DOWN, with no forward order;
- it outgrew the client (root-caused separately);
- it cannot name a group of steps as one route (the Fourier route F1–F5);
- "as before, except one step" cannot be said (Neumann).
The trials' read-back agent IS Tao's class test, but it lives only in the trial method, not in the design.

OPTIONS:
(a) a forward reading order for reasoning_report (setting → definitions → lemmas in dependency order → theorem), with named routes;
(b) a "route" record grouping steps, so a reading can say "proof 2, by the maximum principle";
(c) a check kind for "a fresh reader restated it from the design alone", recorded like any verification, with who read it and what they restated;
(d) nothing new; the agent writes the exposition from the read-back.

PUSHBACK: an exposition is prose a person writes. reflow2 should ORDER and GROUP what it already holds, not generate text. Its credibility rests on reading back what is recorded. (c) risks a check that only ever passes when agents read agents' designs; a person's read-back should be distinguishable.

SIZE (a finding): (a) small to moderate; (b) moderate; (c) small, built on Verification; (d) nothing.

